<section class="section-soft">
<div class="wrap split">
<div class="prose reveal">
<h2 class="h2">The logistics, handled quietly.</h2>
<div class="rule"></div>
<p>Events live and die on timing. We coordinate arrivals to avoid the valet crush, hold the vehicle for the duration when that's the plan, and manage the exit so you're not standing on a curb. For conferences and high-demand weekends, we lock the schedule in advance.</p>
<p>For groups, we coordinate multiple vehicles to keep a party moving together. Tell us the venue and call time; we build the plan backward from it. Covers hotel and venue transportation, VIP and wedding-party movement, and airport arrivals timed to the event itself, not booked as a separate afterthought.</p>
</div>
<div class="figure reveal">
<div class="kicker">On<br>cue.<br><em>Discreet.</em></div>
<p>Galas, conferences, weddings, sporting and entertainment weekends. Single vehicle or coordinated group movement.</p>
<p style="margin-top:16px"><a href="event-art-basel.html" style="color:#B8912E;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500">Art Basel Miami Beach, Dec 4–6 →</a></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section-dark">
<div class="wrap">
<div class="grid-head reveal" style="margin-bottom:28px">
<p class="eyebrow on-dark">Multi-Vehicle &amp; Groups</p>
<h2 class="h2">How a coordinated event day runs.</h2>
<div class="rule"></div>
</div>
<div class="faq reveal">
<details><summary>How does staging work for a group arrival?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">Vehicles are staged ahead of the call time at a confirmed point near the venue, sequenced so the group arrives together rather than trickling in.</div></details>
<details><summary>Is there a single point of contact on the day?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">Yes — one day-of contact coordinates all vehicles and timing, so you're not managing multiple drivers separately if plans shift.</div></details>
<details><summary>Do you need a passenger manifest in advance?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">For multi-vehicle bookings, yes — names and vehicle assignments confirmed ahead of the event avoid confusion at pickup, especially for weddings and large parties.</div></details>
<details><summary>What about the return trip at the end of the night?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">Return timing is planned at booking, not left open-ended — whether that's a fixed pickup time or an on-call window once the event wraps.</div></details>
<details><summary>Who drives if you need more vehicles than you have?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">Onyx's own vehicle is a privately maintained 2026 Chevrolet Suburban RST. When an event needs more vehicles than that, a vetted partner vehicle is arranged and confirmed with you before booking — never a surprise on the day.</div></details>
</div>
</div>
</section>
